{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  Lookbook skeleton — placeholder looks for the lookbook's mount point.

  snippets/lookbook.liquid renders this inside <div data-lookbook>, one
  placeholder per look in the first batch, so the section has its shape from
  the first paint. src/lookbook/index.jsx loads those looks through the
  Storefront API and then mounts React, which replaces these placeholders with
  the looks in a single render.

  A placeholder is shaped like a look in general — a title, a line of text and
  a row of product cards — rather than like one template, because each look's
  template is only known once the API has answered.

  The placeholders are hidden from assistive technology; the visually hidden
  status announces that the lookbook is loading instead.

  ACCEPTS
    looks        how many placeholder looks to draw
    show_header  also draw a placeholder for the section heading
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="lookbook lookbook--skeleton">
  <p class="visually-hidden" role="status">{{ 'accessibility.loading' | t }}</p>

  {%- if show_header -%}
    <div class="lookbook__header page-width" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="lookbook__skeleton-bar lookbook__skeleton-bar--heading"></span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- for look in (1..looks) -%}
    <div class="lookbook__entry lookbook__skeleton page-width" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="lookbook__skeleton-bar lookbook__skeleton-bar--title"></span>
      <span class="lookbook__skeleton-bar lookbook__skeleton-bar--line"></span>
      <div class="lookbook__products lookbook__skeleton-cards">
        {%- for card in (1..4) -%}
          <span class="lookbook__skeleton-card"></span>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>
